  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "298 single-family homes and 38 duplexes (76 units). County status: Complete April 18, 2025, under CEQA review.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001431"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2026 Notice of Preparation describes demolition of existing structures, two parks with pickleball courts and a playground, removal of 28 protected trees with 769 new trees, a detention pond, a public water system with supply wells and two 200,000-gallon tanks, and a community onsite wastewater system with about 2.74 acres of leach fields. Required approvals: major subdivision, grading approval and EIR certification.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002293"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "NBC Bay Area reports the site is Andy's Orchard, owned by the Mariani family, and that Mana Investments holds an option to buy the ranch, with the sale depending on county approval.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002294"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The March 2024 SF YIMBY report gives 374 units (298 single-family homes and 76 duplex units) and about 952,500 sq ft of built area.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002295"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The county's September 2024 incompleteness letter lists the site as 1515 and 1615 Half Road and the application received date as August 21, 2024; the plan set showed 369 trees to be removed, not counting orchard trees.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002296"
      ]
    }
  ],
